# Air Modal CTAs (Pattern A)

One footer hierarchy everywhere. Footer order is always **dismiss · tertiary (optional) · commit**, left to right.

## Rule

| Role | `variant` | `color` | Labels |
|---|---|---|---|
| Dismiss | `outline` | (default primary) | Cancel (forms opposite Save), Keep editing, Close (view-only panels) |
| Tertiary | `text` | `secondary` | Optional, rare (never looks like the primary) |
| Commit | `primary` (contained) | primary | Add, Save, Confirm, Continue |
| Destructive commit | `primary` | `error` | Discard, Delete, Deactivate |

Destructive confirms use a positive stay label (**Keep role**, **Keep account**, **Keep editing**) opposite the error commit. Do not pair **Cancel** with Delete / Discard / Deactivate.

## Disabled commit (forms only)

`disabled: true` until every required field has a non-empty valid value. Re-enable live via `modalApi.setActions(...)`.

## Reference

- API: `DS.modal`, `modalApi.setActions` in `components.js`
